# server_db's settings. Copy to certificates/server_db.env and `chmod 600` it; it never goes in git.
# Values with $, ! or spaces go in single quotes.

# ── Phase 1: the database (ROADMAP) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The LXC's own address on the LAN, fixed: 192.168.50.229/24, set in the LXC and reserved on the router
# (README, "The LXC"). Every machine on 192.168.50.x connects to it. Never a public address, and never
# forwarded by the router.
SDB_BIND=192.168.50.229
# Optional: a name for it on the LAN (a router DNS entry, or /etc/hosts on each machine), put in the
# MONGODB_URI that add-app prints. Empty: the address above.
SDB_HOSTNAME=
# Where the data lives: the LXC's data disk, mounted here.
SDB_DATA=/srv/server-db/data
# MongoDB's cache, in GB: about half the LXC's memory less 0.5 GB. 3.5 on an 8 GB LXC (recommended,
# DESIGN.md "Speed"), 1.5 on a 4 GB one.
SDB_CACHE_GB=3.5
# The administrator, made on the first start. A password: openssl rand -hex 24
SDB_ROOT_USER=admin
SDB_ROOT_PASSWORD=
# Alert when the data disk, or the backup disk, is this full, in percent: the warning before it is full.
SDB_DISK_ALERT=85
# Uptime Kuma: a monitor of type "Push", heartbeat interval 180 s; paste its whole Push URL. Every minute
# the LXC says whether MongoDB is healthy and the disks are not full; silence for 3 minutes is an alert
# too. Empty: no health timer is installed.
SDB_KUMA_HEALTH=

# ── Phase 2: backups (ROADMAP), once Mahoraga runs here. Empty until then: no backup runs ──────────
# Where every backup goes first, every hour, and what the drill restores from: the LXC's backup disk,
# /srv/server-db-backups.
RESTIC_REPOSITORY=
# The copy: a second place, off this server, that every backup is sent to. Tried every 15 minutes; when
# it is off nothing fails, and the next time it is on it gets every backup it missed. Empty: no copy.
#   the PC on the LAN, over SSH (a Host in ~/.ssh/config, README "The PC"):  sftp:backup-pc:/srv/server-db-copy
#   an S3 bucket (R2, B2, AWS):  s3:https://<ACCOUNT_ID>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com/server-db-backups
SDB_COPY_REPOSITORY=
# Only for an S3 bucket. R2 → Manage API tokens → "Object Read & Write", this bucket.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=auto
# Encrypts every backup, in both places. Lose it and no backup can be read: keep a copy in your password
# manager. Make one: openssl rand -base64 36
RESTIC_PASSWORD=
# Uptime Kuma push monitors for them (README, "Alerts"): the backup (interval 5400 s), the Sunday drill
# (691200 s), and each copy that reaches the PC (259200 s: how long the PC may stay off before you hear).
SDB_KUMA_BACKUP=
SDB_KUMA_DRILL=
SDB_KUMA_COPY=
